CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced from R: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A call of a static member function with a deduced return type, of a class
template specialization, converted the member's body under the caller's
template map, where the class's parameter R was unbound ("no match for
symbol 'is_same_v'").  GCC 11's std::visit lost __visit_invoke this way.
